    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33579" root="فرض" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرِيضٌ</span></b>  An arrow <i>having its notch cut;</i> (S, A,
O, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَفْرُوضٌ</span></b> . (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَضِىٌّ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَارِضٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  Also The <i>cud of
the camel;</i> accord. to Kr: but accord. to others
this is called, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرِيض</span> [q. v.], with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ق</span>. (TA.)

